12
00:00:51,920 --> 00:00:55,920
How to talk about salary negotiation and business English.

13
00:00:55,920 --> 00:00:58,240
That is such an important skill.

14
00:00:58,240 --> 00:01:01,280
Many people feel nervous when talking about salary.

15
00:01:01,280 --> 00:01:06,400
Exactly. Even confident professionals sometimes struggle when it comes to discussing money.

16
00:01:06,400 --> 00:01:12,160
And if you don't communicate clearly during salary discussions, you might miss opportunities.

17
00:01:12,160 --> 00:01:17,520
That's right. So today, we're going to help you speak confidently, professionally, and clearly

18
00:01:17,520 --> 00:01:22,960
when negotiating your salary. And we're going to keep everything very practical.

19
00:01:22,960 --> 00:01:26,880
Yes. Real phrases, real examples, and real conversations.

20
00:01:26,880 --> 00:01:33,880
OK. Let's start with a simple question. When does salary negotiation usually happen?

21
00:01:33,880 --> 00:01:40,880
Good question. It usually happens during job interviews, job offers, promotions, or performance reviews.

22
00:01:40,880 --> 00:01:45,880
Exactly. And each situation requires slightly different language.

23
00:01:45,880 --> 00:01:49,880
Let's start with the most common situation, a job interview.

24
00:01:49,880 --> 00:01:54,880
Right. At some point, the interviewer may ask, what are your salary expectations?

25
00:01:54,880 --> 00:02:01,260
patients. This is a very important question. Many people don't know how to answer it. Yes,

26
00:02:01,260 --> 00:02:06,880
and some people make mistakes like giving a number too quickly or sounding unsure. So

27
00:02:06,880 --> 00:02:12,640
what's a good way to respond? You can say, I'm open to discussing salary based on the

28
00:02:12,640 --> 00:02:19,280
role and responsibilities. That's a very professional answer. Another option is,

29
00:02:19,280 --> 00:02:25,020
Based on my experience and the market rate, I'm expecting a salary in the range of...

30
00:02:25,020 --> 00:02:27,980
That shows preparation and confidence.

31
00:02:27,980 --> 00:02:29,820
Let's give a full example.

32
00:02:29,820 --> 00:02:35,020
Sure, based on my experience and industry standards, I'm looking for a salary in the

33
00:02:35,020 --> 00:02:38,740
range of $60,000 to $70,000.

34
00:02:38,740 --> 00:02:41,780
That's clear, realistic, and professional.

35
00:02:41,780 --> 00:02:46,900
Now let's talk about an important strategy, giving a range instead of a single number.

36
00:02:46,900 --> 00:02:51,940
Yes, this gives flexibility and shows that you're open to negotiation.

37
00:02:51,940 --> 00:02:55,540
Exactly. If you give one number, you limit the conversation.

38
00:02:55,540 --> 00:02:58,660
But a range keeps the discussion open.

39
00:02:58,660 --> 00:03:03,380
Now, let's move to another situation when the company makes you an offer.

40
00:03:03,380 --> 00:03:07,300
Yes, this is where negotiation really begins.

41
00:03:07,300 --> 00:03:13,940
Imagine the employer says, we'd like to offer you this position with a salary of $55,000.

42
00:03:13,940 --> 00:03:17,180
What should you say if you want a higher salary?

43
00:03:17,180 --> 00:03:20,020
First, don't say no immediately.

44
00:03:20,020 --> 00:03:23,380
Yes, always show appreciation first.

45
00:03:23,380 --> 00:03:25,500
You can say, thank you for the offer.

46
00:03:25,500 --> 00:03:28,020
I'm really excited about this opportunity.

47
00:03:28,020 --> 00:03:29,620
Then you can continue.

48
00:03:29,620 --> 00:03:33,340
I was hoping for something closer to $65,000

49
00:03:33,340 --> 00:03:34,980
based on my experience.

50
00:03:34,980 --> 00:03:36,900
Is there any flexibility?

51
00:03:36,900 --> 00:03:39,140
That's polite and confident.

52
00:03:39,140 --> 00:03:43,180
Exactly, you're not rejecting, you're negotiating.

53
00:03:43,180 --> 00:03:44,820
Let's do a role play.

54
00:03:44,820 --> 00:03:45,980
Great idea.

55
00:03:45,980 --> 00:03:47,780
We'd like to offer you the position

56
00:03:47,780 --> 00:03:50,420
with a salary of $50,000.

57
00:03:50,420 --> 00:03:51,940
Thank you for the offer.

58
00:03:51,940 --> 00:03:53,500
I really appreciate it.

59
00:03:53,500 --> 00:03:55,620
I'm very interested in the role.

60
00:03:55,620 --> 00:03:58,860
However, based on my experience and skills,

61
00:03:58,860 --> 00:04:02,460
I was expecting something closer to $60,000.

62
00:04:02,460 --> 00:04:04,180
Is there any flexibility?

63
00:04:04,180 --> 00:04:05,140
That's excellent.

64
00:04:05,140 --> 00:04:07,420
Very professional and respectful.

65
00:04:07,420 --> 00:04:11,500
Notice the structure, appreciation, expectation,

66
00:04:11,500 --> 00:04:12,860
and question.

67
00:04:12,860 --> 00:04:15,360
Yes, that's a powerful formula.

68
00:04:15,360 --> 00:04:19,160
Now let's talk about justifying your salary request.

69
00:04:19,160 --> 00:04:20,840
This is very important.

70
00:04:20,840 --> 00:04:24,400
You need to explain why you deserve a higher salary.

71
00:04:24,400 --> 00:04:26,560
You can mention your experience.

72
00:04:26,560 --> 00:04:29,120
For example, I have over five years

73
00:04:29,120 --> 00:04:31,040
of experience in this field.

74
00:04:31,040 --> 00:04:32,920
You can mention your skills.

75
00:04:32,920 --> 00:04:35,560
I have strong skills in project management

76
00:04:35,560 --> 00:04:37,160
and team leadership.

77
00:04:37,160 --> 00:04:39,680
And you can mention achievements.

78
00:04:39,680 --> 00:04:40,880
In my previous role,

79
00:04:40,880 --> 00:04:44,100
I increased sales by 30 percent.

80
00:04:44,100 --> 00:04:46,320
Let's combine everything.

81
00:04:46,320 --> 00:04:51,800
Based on my experience, my skill set, and my previous results, I believe a higher salary

82
00:04:51,800 --> 00:04:53,600
would be appropriate.

83
00:04:53,600 --> 00:04:55,640
That sounds very convincing.

84
00:04:55,640 --> 00:05:01,240
Now let's talk about another situation, negotiating your salary in your current job.

85
00:05:01,240 --> 00:05:04,840
Yes, for example, during a performance review.

86
00:05:04,840 --> 00:05:09,220
Your manager might ask, do you have any questions or requests?

87
00:05:09,220 --> 00:05:11,100
This is your opportunity.

88
00:05:11,100 --> 00:05:14,780
You can say, I'd like to discuss my compensation.

89
00:05:14,780 --> 00:05:18,780
Or I'd like to talk about a possible salary adjustment.

90
00:05:18,780 --> 00:05:21,020
Then explain your reasons.

91
00:05:21,020 --> 00:05:26,220
Over the past year, I've taken on additional responsibilities and contributed to several

92
00:05:26,220 --> 00:05:28,220
successful projects.

93
00:05:28,220 --> 00:05:29,860
That's a strong argument.

94
00:05:29,860 --> 00:05:33,220
Yes, always focus on value.

95
00:05:33,220 --> 00:05:34,940
Let's do another role play.

96
00:05:34,940 --> 00:05:35,940
Okay.

97
00:05:35,940 --> 00:05:38,340
So, how do you feel about your current role?

98
00:05:38,340 --> 00:05:40,980
I'm very happy with my role and the team.

99
00:05:40,980 --> 00:05:42,300
I've learned a lot.

100
00:05:42,300 --> 00:05:44,860
I'd also like to discuss my compensation

101
00:05:44,860 --> 00:05:48,300
as I've taken on more responsibilities over the past year.

102
00:05:48,300 --> 00:05:50,980
That's a great way to introduce the topic.

103
00:05:50,980 --> 00:05:54,220
Now let's talk about negotiating benefits.

104
00:05:54,220 --> 00:05:57,780
Yes, salary is not the only thing you can negotiate.

105
00:05:57,780 --> 00:06:01,420
You can also discuss bonuses, vacation days,

106
00:06:01,420 --> 00:06:04,660
flexible working hours, or remote work options.

107
00:06:04,660 --> 00:06:05,780
Exactly.

108
00:06:05,780 --> 00:06:11,860
For example, if the salary is fixed, would it be possible to discuss additional benefits?

109
00:06:11,860 --> 00:06:14,980
Or would there be flexibility in terms of remote work?

110
00:06:15,700 --> 00:06:18,500
That shows you're flexible and solution-oriented.

111
00:06:19,060 --> 00:06:20,820
Now let's talk about confidence.

112
00:06:21,460 --> 00:06:23,460
Yes, this is key.

113
00:06:23,460 --> 00:06:28,020
Even if your English is not perfect, speak clearly and calmly.

114
00:06:28,020 --> 00:06:29,780
Avoid sounding unsure.

115
00:06:30,340 --> 00:06:35,300
For example, don't say, maybe, I think, if possible, too much.

116
00:06:35,780 --> 00:06:40,260
Instead, say, I believe or I would expect.

117
00:06:40,260 --> 00:06:41,820
That sounds stronger.

118
00:06:41,820 --> 00:06:44,420
Now let's talk about common mistakes.

119
00:06:44,420 --> 00:06:47,220
Yes, this is very important.

120
00:06:47,220 --> 00:06:51,220
Mistake one is accepting the first offer immediately.

121
00:06:51,220 --> 00:06:53,500
Always take time to think.

122
00:06:53,500 --> 00:06:56,060
Mistake two is being too aggressive.

123
00:06:56,060 --> 00:06:58,740
Yes, negotiation is not a fight.

124
00:06:58,740 --> 00:07:00,500
It's a conversation.

125
00:07:00,500 --> 00:07:03,300
Mistake three is not doing research.

126
00:07:03,300 --> 00:07:06,460
You should know the market salary for your role.

127
00:07:06,460 --> 00:07:09,340
Mistake 4 is focusing only on money.

128
00:07:09,340 --> 00:07:11,980
Remember, benefits also matter.

129
00:07:11,980 --> 00:07:15,380
Now let's do a longer real-life conversation.

130
00:07:15,380 --> 00:07:16,380
Great.

131
00:07:16,380 --> 00:07:17,380
Thank you for the offer.

132
00:07:17,380 --> 00:07:20,100
I'm very excited about this opportunity.

133
00:07:20,100 --> 00:07:21,900
We're happy to have you on board.

134
00:07:21,900 --> 00:07:24,340
I'd like to discuss the salary.

135
00:07:24,340 --> 00:07:28,700
Based on my experience and the responsibilities of the role, I was expecting something

136
00:07:28,700 --> 00:07:30,500
slightly higher.

137
00:07:30,500 --> 00:07:32,180
What range are you considering?

138
00:07:32,180 --> 00:07:36,880
I was thinking of a range between $70,000 and $80,000.

139
00:07:36,880 --> 00:07:39,040
That's a bit above our budget.

140
00:07:39,040 --> 00:07:40,260
I understand.

141
00:07:40,260 --> 00:07:44,060
Is there flexibility in the overall compensation package,

142
00:07:44,060 --> 00:07:46,780
such as bonuses or additional benefits?

143
00:07:46,780 --> 00:07:49,340
We can discuss a performance bonus.

144
00:07:49,340 --> 00:07:50,540
That sounds great.

145
00:07:50,540 --> 00:07:52,340
I'd be happy to consider that.

146
00:07:52,340 --> 00:07:55,220
That's an excellent example of negotiation.

147
00:07:55,220 --> 00:07:59,380
Yes, it's respectful, flexible, and professional.

148
00:07:59,380 --> 00:08:02,420
Now, let's talk about ending the negotiation.

149
00:08:02,420 --> 00:08:05,620
Yes, always end positively.

150
00:08:05,620 --> 00:08:09,060
You can say, thank you for taking the time to discuss this.

151
00:08:09,060 --> 00:08:12,020
Or, I appreciate your consideration.

152
00:08:12,020 --> 00:08:13,980
This leaves a good impression.

153
00:08:13,980 --> 00:08:16,020
Now, let's summarize.

154
00:08:16,020 --> 00:08:18,820
First, be prepared and know your value.

155
00:08:18,820 --> 00:08:22,220
Second, use clear and professional language.

156
00:08:22,220 --> 00:08:24,900
Third, be confident but polite.

157
00:08:24,900 --> 00:08:28,980
Fourth, be open to negotiation and alternatives.

158
00:08:28,980 --> 00:08:31,940
And remember, negotiation is normal.

159
00:08:31,940 --> 00:08:35,940
Yes, it's expected in many professional situations.

160
00:08:35,940 --> 00:08:38,500
So don't be afraid to speak up.

161
00:08:38,500 --> 00:08:41,660
Your skills and experience have value.

162
00:08:41,660 --> 00:08:43,980
Now it's your turn to practice.

163
00:08:43,980 --> 00:08:48,460
Try saying, based on my experience, I'm expecting...

164
00:08:48,460 --> 00:08:50,660
Try it until it feels natural.

165
00:08:50,660 --> 00:08:52,940
Thank you so much for listening.

166
00:08:52,940 --> 00:08:55,260
We hope this helps you feel more confident

167
00:08:55,260 --> 00:08:57,260
in salary negotiations.

