On this channel, we help you speak clear, natural English with confidence in professional environments.

929
00:45:17,780 --> 00:45:22,420
If you enjoy this lesson, don't forget to give us a thumbs up and subscribe.

930
00:45:22,420 --> 00:45:26,580
Your support really helps us continue creating content like this.

931
00:45:26,580 --> 00:45:28,820
Yes, thank you so much for being here.

932
00:45:28,820 --> 00:45:31,300
So, Olivia, what are we talking about today?

933
00:45:31,300 --> 00:45:37,820
But today you were focusing on a topic that many people find stressful but extremely important,

934
00:45:37,820 --> 00:45:41,180
how to talk about salary negotiation in English.

935
00:45:41,180 --> 00:45:43,420
Oh wow, that's a big one.

936
00:45:43,420 --> 00:45:48,180
I think a lot of people feel nervous when they hear the words salary negotiation.

937
00:45:48,180 --> 00:45:49,660
Absolutely.

938
00:45:49,660 --> 00:45:55,420
Even native speakers sometimes feel uncomfortable talking about money, especially in professional

939
00:45:55,420 --> 00:45:56,420
situations.

940
00:45:56,420 --> 00:45:57,660
That's true.

941
00:45:57,660 --> 00:46:00,660
But at the same time, it's such an important skill.

942
00:46:00,660 --> 00:46:04,260
If you don't talk about your salary, you might miss opportunities.

943
00:46:04,260 --> 00:46:05,660
Exactly.

944
00:46:05,660 --> 00:46:11,060
Learning how to communicate clearly and confidently about salary can make a huge difference in

945
00:46:11,060 --> 00:46:12,060
your career.

946
00:46:12,060 --> 00:46:16,580
So, today we're going to help everyone feel more comfortable and prepared.

947
00:46:16,580 --> 00:46:22,540
Yes, we'll teach useful phrases, practical examples, and real conversations so you

948
00:46:22,540 --> 00:46:25,980
can negotiate professionally and confidently.

949
00:46:25,980 --> 00:46:26,980
Sounds amazing.

950
00:46:26,980 --> 00:46:29,740
So, Olivia, before we start, how are you feeling today?

951
00:46:29,740 --> 00:46:31,180
I'm feeling great.

952
00:46:31,180 --> 00:46:35,940
I'm excited about this topic because I know it will really help our listeners.

953
00:46:35,940 --> 00:46:36,940
How about you?

954
00:46:36,940 --> 00:46:37,940
I'm doing well.

955
00:46:37,940 --> 00:46:41,420
I had a busy morning, but I'm ready to dive into this lesson.

956
00:46:41,420 --> 00:46:42,420
Perfect.

957
00:46:42,420 --> 00:46:43,420
Let's get started.

958
00:46:43,420 --> 00:46:46,620
Okay, Olivia, let's begin with something simple.

959
00:46:46,620 --> 00:46:49,900
When does salary negotiation usually happen?

960
00:46:49,900 --> 00:46:51,300
Good question.

961
00:46:51,300 --> 00:46:54,660
Salary negotiation can happen in different situations.

962
00:46:54,660 --> 00:47:00,160
For example, during a job interview, after receiving a job offer, or when asking for

963
00:47:00,160 --> 00:47:01,160
a raise.

964
00:47:01,160 --> 00:47:03,600
Right, so it's not just for new jobs.

965
00:47:03,600 --> 00:47:06,840
You can also negotiate your salary in your current job.

966
00:47:06,840 --> 00:47:07,840
Exactly.

967
00:47:07,840 --> 00:47:12,440
And the language you use is very important in all these situations.

968
00:47:12,440 --> 00:47:15,320
So let's start with a common situation.

969
00:47:15,320 --> 00:47:16,560
Receiving a job offer.

970
00:47:16,560 --> 00:47:17,840
What happens next?

971
00:47:17,840 --> 00:47:21,520
Usually, the company will tell you the salary they are offering.

972
00:47:21,520 --> 00:47:24,160
Then you can accept it or negotiate.

973
00:47:24,160 --> 00:47:26,960
And many people are afraid to negotiate, right?

974
00:47:26,960 --> 00:47:32,160
Yes, they think it's rude or risky, but actually it's very normal in business.

975
00:47:32,160 --> 00:47:33,800
That's a great point.

976
00:47:33,800 --> 00:47:37,500
So how can someone start a salary negotiation politely?

977
00:47:37,500 --> 00:47:40,480
You can use soft and professional language.

978
00:47:40,480 --> 00:47:43,520
For example, you can say, thank you for the offer.

979
00:47:43,520 --> 00:47:46,080
I'm really excited about this opportunity.

980
00:47:46,080 --> 00:47:49,280
I was wondering if we could discuss the salary.

981
00:47:49,280 --> 00:47:50,880
That sounds very polite.

982
00:47:50,880 --> 00:47:54,240
showing appreciation and then asking to negotiate.

983
00:47:54,240 --> 00:47:58,240
Exactly. It's important to sound positive and respectful.

984
00:47:58,240 --> 00:48:02,320
Let's give more examples. What are some other ways to start the conversation?

985
00:48:02,320 --> 00:48:05,840
Sure. You could say, I appreciate the offer.

986
00:48:05,840 --> 00:48:10,320
Based on my experience, I was expecting something slightly higher.

987
00:48:10,320 --> 00:48:13,680
Nice. That sounds confident but not aggressive.

988
00:48:13,680 --> 00:48:18,800
Yes. Or you could say, is there any flexibility in the salary range?

989
00:48:18,800 --> 00:48:21,800
Oh, I like that one. It's simple and direct.

990
00:48:21,800 --> 00:48:26,800
Another example is, I'd like to discuss the compensation package in more detail.

991
00:48:26,800 --> 00:48:29,800
Compensation package? That's a useful phrase.

992
00:48:29,800 --> 00:48:34,800
Yes. It includes salary, bonuses, benefits, and more.

993
00:48:34,800 --> 00:48:40,800
Now, let's talk about giving reasons. Why is it important to explain why you want a higher salary?

994
00:48:40,800 --> 00:48:47,800
Because it shows that your request is reasonable. You're not just asking for more money, you have a reason.

995
00:48:47,800 --> 00:48:51,080
So, what kind of reasons can people give?

996
00:48:51,080 --> 00:48:55,060
You can mention your experience, skills, or the market rate.

997
00:48:55,060 --> 00:49:00,800
For example, I have five years of experience in this field, and I bring strong skills in

998
00:49:00,800 --> 00:49:02,520
project management.

999
00:49:02,520 --> 00:49:04,120
That's a strong argument.

1000
00:49:04,120 --> 00:49:10,360
Or you can say, based on industry standards, I believe a higher salary would be appropriate.

1001
00:49:10,360 --> 00:49:12,240
That sounds very professional.

1002
00:49:12,240 --> 00:49:15,360
Yes, you can also mention your achievements.

1003
00:49:15,360 --> 00:49:20,600
For example, in my previous role, I increased sales by 20%.

1004
00:49:20,600 --> 00:49:21,920
That's impressive.

1005
00:49:21,920 --> 00:49:23,440
Numbers always help.

1006
00:49:23,440 --> 00:49:24,440
Exactly.

1007
00:49:24,440 --> 00:49:26,640
Now, let's do a quick role play.

1008
00:49:26,640 --> 00:49:29,520
I'll be the employer and you'll be the candidate.

1009
00:49:29,520 --> 00:49:30,520
Sounds good.

1010
00:49:30,520 --> 00:49:31,520
Let's do it.

1011
00:49:31,520 --> 00:49:32,520
Congratulations, Olivia.

1012
00:49:32,520 --> 00:49:37,120
We'd like to offer you the position with a salary of $50,000 per year.

1013
00:49:37,120 --> 00:49:38,120
Thank you so much.

1014
00:49:38,120 --> 00:49:40,520
I'm really excited about the opportunity.

1015
00:49:40,520 --> 00:49:43,360
I was wondering if we could discuss the salary.

1016
00:49:43,360 --> 00:49:45,600
Of course, what do you have in mind?

1017
00:49:45,600 --> 00:49:49,720
Based on my experience and the responsibilities of this role,

1018
00:49:49,720 --> 00:49:53,440
I was expecting something closer to $60,000.

1019
00:49:53,440 --> 00:49:54,160
I see.

1020
00:49:54,160 --> 00:49:56,640
That's a bit higher than our initial offer.

1021
00:49:56,640 --> 00:49:57,720
I understand.

1022
00:49:57,720 --> 00:49:59,800
I'm open to discussing it further.

1023
00:49:59,800 --> 00:50:01,880
I believe my skills and experience

1024
00:50:01,880 --> 00:50:04,200
would bring strong value to the team.

1025
00:50:04,200 --> 00:50:06,800
Let me check with the team and see what we can do.

1026
00:50:06,800 --> 00:50:07,440
Thank you.

1027
00:50:07,440 --> 00:50:08,760
I appreciate that.

1028
00:50:08,760 --> 00:50:10,000
That was excellent.

1029
00:50:10,000 --> 00:50:10,680
Thank you.

1030
00:50:10,680 --> 00:50:12,200
It felt realistic.

1031
00:50:12,200 --> 00:50:14,880
Now, let's talk about another situation.

1032
00:50:14,880 --> 00:50:17,640
Asking for a raise in your current job.

1033
00:50:17,640 --> 00:50:19,600
This can be even more difficult

1034
00:50:19,600 --> 00:50:23,000
because you already have a relationship with your manager.

1035
00:50:23,000 --> 00:50:26,280
Right, so how can someone start that conversation?

1036
00:50:26,280 --> 00:50:28,840
You can say, I'd like to schedule a meeting

1037
00:50:28,840 --> 00:50:31,800
to discuss my performance and compensation.

1038
00:50:31,800 --> 00:50:33,880
That sounds very professional.

1039
00:50:33,880 --> 00:50:37,120
Or you can say, I'd like to talk about the possibility

1040
00:50:37,120 --> 00:50:38,840
of a salary increase.

1041
00:50:38,840 --> 00:50:40,240
Simple and clear.

1042
00:50:40,240 --> 00:50:43,360
During the meeting, you should explain your value.

1043
00:50:43,360 --> 00:50:48,600
For example, over the past year, I've taken on additional responsibilities and contributed

1044
00:50:48,600 --> 00:50:50,800
to several successful projects.

1045
00:50:50,800 --> 00:50:51,800
That's good.

1046
00:50:51,800 --> 00:50:53,480
You're showing what you've done.

1047
00:50:53,480 --> 00:50:54,480
Yes.

1048
00:50:54,480 --> 00:51:00,400
Then you can say, I'd like to discuss adjusting my salary to reflect my contributions.

1049
00:51:00,400 --> 00:51:01,400
Very nice.

1050
00:51:01,400 --> 00:51:03,440
Let's do another role play.

1051
00:51:03,440 --> 00:51:05,480
This time, you're the employee.

1052
00:51:05,480 --> 00:51:06,480
Okay.

1053
00:51:06,480 --> 00:51:07,480
I'm ready.

1054
00:51:07,480 --> 00:51:08,480
Hi, Olivia.

1055
00:51:08,480 --> 00:51:09,480
Thanks for meeting with me.

1056
00:51:09,480 --> 00:51:11,480
Of course. What would you like to discuss?

1057
00:51:11,480 --> 00:51:15,480
I wanted to talk about my performance and my salary.

1058
00:51:15,480 --> 00:51:18,480
Over the past year, I've taken on more responsibilities

1059
00:51:18,480 --> 00:51:20,480
and helped improve our team's results.

1060
00:51:20,480 --> 00:51:23,480
Yes, I've noticed your contributions.

1061
00:51:23,480 --> 00:51:27,480
Thank you. I was hoping we could discuss a possible salary increase

1062
00:51:27,480 --> 00:51:28,480
that reflects my work.

1063
00:51:28,480 --> 00:51:30,480
That's a reasonable request.

1064
00:51:30,480 --> 00:51:34,480
Let me review your performance and we can continue this conversation.

1065
00:51:34,480 --> 00:51:36,480
I appreciate that. Thank you.

1066
00:51:36,480 --> 00:51:38,480
That was excellent.

1067
00:51:38,480 --> 00:51:40,520
Thank you, it felt realistic.

1068
00:51:40,520 --> 00:51:44,640
Now let's talk about negotiating benefits, not just salary.

1069
00:51:44,640 --> 00:51:46,580
Oh yes, that's important.

1070
00:51:46,580 --> 00:51:51,040
Sometimes the company can't increase salary, but they can offer other benefits.

1071
00:51:51,040 --> 00:51:52,040
Exactly.

1072
00:51:52,040 --> 00:51:58,240
For example, you can negotiate flexible hours, remote work, or extra vacation days.

1073
00:51:58,240 --> 00:51:59,760
So what can you say?

1074
00:51:59,760 --> 00:52:05,480
You can say, if the salary is fixed, would it be possible to discuss other benefits?

1075
00:52:05,480 --> 00:52:06,480
That's smart.

1076
00:52:06,480 --> 00:52:12,160
Or you can say, would there be flexibility in terms of remote work or additional vacation

1077
00:52:12,160 --> 00:52:13,160
time?

1078
00:52:13,160 --> 00:52:14,560
Very useful phrases.

1079
00:52:14,560 --> 00:52:17,280
Now let's talk about common mistakes.

1080
00:52:17,280 --> 00:52:18,600
This is important.

1081
00:52:18,600 --> 00:52:22,320
Many people make mistakes when negotiating salary.

1082
00:52:22,320 --> 00:52:26,840
Mistake number one, being too direct, saying, I want more money.

1083
00:52:26,840 --> 00:52:29,040
Yes, that sounds aggressive.

1084
00:52:29,040 --> 00:52:33,120
Instead, say, I was hoping for a higher salary.

1085
00:52:33,120 --> 00:52:35,760
Mistake number two, not giving reasons.

1086
00:52:35,760 --> 00:52:38,080
Right. You need to explain why.

1087
00:52:38,080 --> 00:52:41,080
Mistake number three, sounding negative.

1088
00:52:41,080 --> 00:52:43,920
For example, this salary is too low.

1089
00:52:43,920 --> 00:52:47,680
Better to say, I was expecting a higher range.

1090
00:52:47,680 --> 00:52:50,760
Mistake number four, not being prepared.

1091
00:52:50,760 --> 00:52:53,760
You should research the market before negotiating.

1092
00:52:53,760 --> 00:52:57,080
Mistake number five, accepting too quickly.

1093
00:52:57,080 --> 00:52:59,920
Yes. Sometimes you should take time to think.

1094
00:52:59,920 --> 00:53:03,160
Exactly. You can say, thank you for the offer.

1095
00:53:03,160 --> 00:53:05,120
I'd like some time to review it.

1096
00:53:05,120 --> 00:53:06,720
That's a great phrase.

1097
00:53:06,720 --> 00:53:11,440
Now let's do one more detailed role play with a full negotiation.

1098
00:53:11,440 --> 00:53:12,960
Perfect. Let's go.

1099
00:53:12,960 --> 00:53:17,840
We're happy to offer you the position with a salary of $55,000.

1100
00:53:17,840 --> 00:53:21,440
Thank you. I'm very excited about the role and the company.

1101
00:53:21,440 --> 00:53:24,240
I'd like to discuss the salary if possible.

1102
00:53:24,240 --> 00:53:26,640
Sure. What are your expectations?

1103
00:53:26,640 --> 00:53:29,920
Based on my experience and the industry standards,

1104
00:53:29,920 --> 00:53:35,200
I was expecting something in the range of $60,000 to $65,000.

1105
00:53:35,200 --> 00:53:37,280
That's slightly above our budget.

1106
00:53:37,280 --> 00:53:41,760
I understand. Is there any flexibility in the compensation package?

1107
00:53:41,760 --> 00:53:46,160
We might be able to offer a signing bonus or additional vacation days.

1108
00:53:46,160 --> 00:53:49,840
That would be great. I'd be open to discussing those options.

1109
00:53:49,840 --> 00:53:52,000
Let me review this and get back to you.

1110
00:53:52,000 --> 00:53:55,200
Thank you. I really appreciate your consideration.

1111
00:53:55,200 --> 00:53:58,720
That was excellent. Very natural and professional.

1112
00:53:58,720 --> 00:53:59,600
Thank you.

1113
00:53:59,600 --> 00:54:02,400
Now let's wrap up with some final tips.

1114
00:54:02,400 --> 00:54:05,600
First, always be polite and professional.

1115
00:54:05,600 --> 00:54:08,800
Second, be confident but not aggressive.

1116
00:54:08,800 --> 00:54:12,100
Third, give clear reasons for your request.

1117
00:54:12,100 --> 00:54:15,500
Fourth, be open to discussion and compromise.

1118
00:54:15,500 --> 00:54:19,300
And finally, practice your English before the conversation.

1119
00:54:19,300 --> 00:54:23,600
Practice is key. The more you practice, the more confident you'll feel.

1120
00:54:23,600 --> 00:54:25,000
Absolutely.

1121
00:54:25,000 --> 00:54:27,600
Now it's time for our question of the day.

1122
00:54:27,600 --> 00:54:31,280
Have you ever negotiated your salary? What did you say?

1123
00:54:31,280 --> 00:54:35,440
Or if you haven't, what would you say in a salary negotiation?

1124
00:54:35,440 --> 00:54:38,320
Write your answers and practice your sentences.

1125
00:54:38,320 --> 00:54:41,520
Don't be afraid of making mistakes. That's how you learn.

1126
00:54:41,520 --> 00:54:44,000
Thank you so much for being here with us today.

1127
00:54:44,000 --> 00:54:47,840
If you enjoyed this lesson, don't forget to like and subscribe.

1128
00:54:47,840 --> 00:54:51,200
Keep practicing, keep improving, and stay confident.

1129
00:54:51,200 --> 00:54:53,520
We'll see you in the next episode.

1130
00:54:53,520 --> 00:54:54,720
Goodbye, everyone.

1131
00:54:54,720 --> 00:54:55,440
Goodbye.
